=begin
  timers_sagapanel.lic

  Saga-only panel listing everything currently active: Active Spells (via
  Spell.active, lib/common/spell.rb -- the same thing
  Lich::Gemstone::Spells.active/"spell active" report, not the Active
  Spells dialog feed, which can under-report depending on your spell-name
  display preference), plus Effects::Buffs, Effects::Debuffs, and
  Effects::Cooldowns (lib/gemstone/effects.rb) for the other three. All
  read live, not parsed by this script. Each section only appears while it
  has at least one entry. Durations show as Saga's own h:mm:ss/m:ss
  convention.

  Spell.active includes some things the game's own dialogs categorize as a
  Buff rather than an Active Spell (Celerity being the one that surfaced
  this -- it's mechanically a spell but only ever appears in the native
  Buffs dialog), so anything currently claimed by Buffs/Debuffs/Cooldowns
  is excluded from Active Spells here -- each name only ever shows in one
  section, matching the game's own categorization rather than Lich's
  internal one.
  Each row shows its category's icon on the left (checkmark/up-arrow/
  warning/alarm-clock for Active Spells/Buffs/Debuffs/Cooldowns), the name
  (clickable -- see below), the duration, then a small red triangle on the
  far right. Category headers are clickable too: "<icon> <Category> -
  Click to Track All" adds every currently-active name in that category to
  your watch list in one go (see below), wherever Spell[] can resolve it.
  *tm headers turns these header rows off entirely if you don't want them
  (each row's own icon still identifies its category either way).

  Also supports a custom watch list: track a spell by name or number
  (or click its name in any of the 4 live categories, or click a category
  header to bulk-add everything in it), and if it's not currently active,
  it shows up in a "Missing Spells" section (top or bottom, your choice)
  instead of the 4 live categories -- so you can see at a glance what you
  meant to have up but don't.

  The red triangle on a live entry (spell/buff/debuff/cooldown) hides that
  name from the panel from then on, even while it's active. The red
  triangle on a missing entry removes it from your watch list entirely
  (stops tracking it, rather than just hiding it).

  Hiding something with the red triangle only affects display -- it does
  NOT exclude it from track-all operations (*tm track all,
  *tm trackall <category>, clicking a category header). Those always scan
  every actually-active spell/buff/debuff/cooldown, ignored or not, so a
  hidden entry you deliberately *tm track by name/number still gets swept
  up the next time you track-all.

  Recast macros: *tm <#> <command chain> registers a ">"-separated chain of
  commands against a spell number, e.g.
    *tm 509 chain 1 store all > get white crystal > rub my white crystal > stow my white crystal
  Once registered, that spell's name in Missing Spells becomes clickable
  (instead of plain text) and runs the whole chain, one command per ">"
  step, with a short pause between each. *tm macros lists what's
  registered; *tm clearmacro <#> removes one. Handy for spells that need
  more than just casting to bring back up (e.g. a prep item to rub after
  recasting).

  Usage:
    ;timers_sagapanel.lic   - Start the panel

  Commands:
    *tm track <name or #>    - Watch a spell; shows in Missing Spells
                                whenever it isn't currently active (same as
                                clicking its name in a live category)
    *tm track all              - Watch everything currently active across
                                all 4 categories (the same set "spell
                                active" reports), wherever Spell[] can
                                resolve it
    *tm untrack <name or #>  - Stop watching a spell (same as clicking the
                                red triangle on a Missing Spells entry)
    *tm untrack all            - Stop watching everything
    *tm tracked               - List your watched spells, grouped under
                                spell circle headers (Minor Spiritual,
                                Empath Base, etc.), number first within
                                each group (e.g. "218 Spirit Servant")
    *tm ignore <name>         - Hide a name from the live categories (same
                                as clicking the red triangle on a live entry)
    *tm unignore <name>       - Un-hide a previously ignored name
    *tm unignore all           - Un-hide everything currently hidden
    *tm ignored                - List currently hidden names, grouped by
                                spell circle the same way as *tm tracked
                                (anything that isn't a real spell lists
                                under "Other")
    *tm missing top            - Show Missing Spells above the 4 categories
    *tm missing bottom         - Show Missing Spells below the 4 categories
    *tm sort az                - Sort each category alphabetically, A-Z
    *tm sort za                - Sort each category alphabetically, Z-A
    *tm sort dhigh              - Sort each category by duration, highest
                                first
    *tm sort dlow                - Sort each category by duration, lowest
                                first
    *tm display name           - Panel rows show just the name (default)
    *tm display number          - Panel rows show just the spell number
                                (falls back to the name for anything
                                Spell[] can't resolve, e.g. most buffs/
                                debuffs)
    *tm display both             - Panel rows show number and name
                                together (same fallback as above)
    *tm pheaders                 - Toggle spell circle sub-headers within
                                each of the 4 live categories in the panel
                                itself (off by default), same grouping as
                                *tm tracked/*tm ignored -- anything that
                                isn't a real spell lists under "Other"
    *tm headers                  - Toggle the main "<icon> Category -
                                Click to Track All" header row per category
                                (on by default). Each row's own icon still
                                identifies its category either way.
    *tm <#> <command chain>   - Register a recast macro for a spell number
                                (see above); makes its name in Missing
                                Spells clickable
    *tm run <#>                 - Run a spell's registered macro (same as
                                clicking its name in Missing Spells)
    *tm clearmacro <#>          - Remove a spell's registered macro
    *tm macros                  - List all registered macros

  Tags: saga, frontend, mod, window, spells, buffs, debuffs, cooldowns
  Author: Claude, RuseofFools
  Version: 1.0.0
  Recently changed:
=end

no_kill_all

require 'yaml'

unless $frontend == 'saga'
  respond ""
  respond " timers relies on a Saga-specific dialog window and will"
  respond " not work correctly on other frontends."
  respond ""
  exit
end

module Timers
  extend self
  include Lich::Common if defined?(Lich::Common)

  ROW_HEIGHT = 18
  ICON_WIDTH = 16
  NAME_LEFT = 18
  NAME_WIDTH = 164
  # 4 characters (~7px each) tighter than the original 210, so the duration
  # sits closer to the name instead of floating in a wide gap.
  DURATION_LEFT = 182
  # Tight enough for "h:mm:ss" (7 chars, the longest format this ever
  # shows) plus a hair of padding -- DURATION_WIDTH used to be 80, leaving
  # a wide dead gap before the removal triangle since real duration text
  # rarely fills that much space.
  DURATION_WIDTH = 45
  # Right after the duration -- see REMOVE_ICON below.
  REMOVE_LEFT = DURATION_LEFT + DURATION_WIDTH + 2
  REMOVE_WIDTH = 20

  # One icon per category, used two ways: prefixed onto the header text
  # (CATEGORY_LABELS) and shown standalone on the left of every row in that
  # category, in the slot the removal X used to occupy -- so at a glance
  # each row's category is identifiable without reading the header it's
  # grouped under.
  CATEGORY_ICONS = {
    spells:    "&#x2705;",
    buffs:     "&#x2B06;&#xFE0F;",
    debuffs:   "&#x26A0;&#xFE0F;",
    cooldowns: "&#x23F0;"
  }.freeze
  # Clickable (see build_dialog/UpstreamHook "*tm trackall") -- clicking a
  # header attempts to Spell[] every name currently in that category and
  # adds whichever resolve to real spells to the watch list in one go.
  CATEGORY_LABELS = {
    spells:    "#{CATEGORY_ICONS[:spells]} Active Spells - Click to Track All",
    buffs:     "#{CATEGORY_ICONS[:buffs]} Buffs - Click to Track All",
    debuffs:   "#{CATEGORY_ICONS[:debuffs]} Debuffs - Click to Track All",
    cooldowns: "#{CATEGORY_ICONS[:cooldowns]} Cooldown - Click to Track All"
  }.freeze
  CATEGORY_ORDER = [:spells, :buffs, :debuffs, :cooldowns].freeze

  MISSING_ICON = "&#x2757;".freeze
  # Down-pointing red triangle -- replaces the old X entirely, moved to the
  # far right of each row (after the duration) instead of the left, since
  # the left slot now holds the category icon.
  REMOVE_ICON = "&#x1F53B;".freeze

  # No "unless defined?" guard -- this module persists in Lich's Ruby
  # process across script restarts (only killing Lich itself clears it), so
  # a guard would freeze this constant at whatever shape it had the first
  # time the script loaded this session. See the identical reasoning in
  # effectsbar_sagapanel.lic.
  SORT_MODES = %w[name_asc name_desc duration_asc duration_desc].freeze
  # *tm display name/number/both -- how every row's name column renders.
  # "number"/"both" fall back to the plain name for anything Spell[]
  # can't resolve to a real spell number (most buffs/debuffs aren't
  # spells), so nothing ever renders blank.
  NAME_DISPLAYS = %w[name number both].freeze

  ST_DEFAULT_SETTINGS = {
    "timers" => {
      "tracked" => [],
      "ignored" => [],
      "missing_position" => "top",
      "sort_mode" => "name_asc",
      "name_display" => "name",
      "panel_headers" => false,
      "macros" => {},
      "category_headers" => true
    }
  }

  class << self
    attr_accessor :tracked, :ignored, :missing_position, :sort_mode, :name_display, :panel_headers, :macros,
                  :category_headers
  end

  def self.window_settings_path(name: Char.name)
    base_dir = "#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}/#{name}"
    Dir.mkdir("#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}") unless File.exist?("#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}")
    Dir.mkdir(base_dir) unless File.exist?(base_dir)
    File.join(base_dir, "lichwindows.yaml")
  end

  def self.load_window_settings
    filename = Timers.window_settings_path
    settings_hash = File.exist?(filename) ? YAML.load_file(filename) : {}
    settings_hash = {} unless settings_hash.is_a?(Hash)
    settings_hash["timers"] = Timers::ST_DEFAULT_SETTINGS["timers"].merge(settings_hash["timers"] || {})
    settings_hash["timers"]["tracked"] = Array(settings_hash["timers"]["tracked"]).map(&:to_i).uniq
    settings_hash["timers"]["ignored"] = Array(settings_hash["timers"]["ignored"]).map { |name| Timers.key(name) }.uniq
    unless %w[top bottom].include?(settings_hash["timers"]["missing_position"])
      settings_hash["timers"]["missing_position"] = "top"
    end
    unless Timers::SORT_MODES.include?(settings_hash["timers"]["sort_mode"])
      settings_hash["timers"]["sort_mode"] = "name_asc"
    end
    unless Timers::NAME_DISPLAYS.include?(settings_hash["timers"]["name_display"])
      settings_hash["timers"]["name_display"] = "name"
    end
    settings_hash["timers"]["panel_headers"] = !!settings_hash["timers"]["panel_headers"]
    raw_macros = settings_hash["timers"]["macros"]
    raw_macros = {} unless raw_macros.is_a?(Hash)
    settings_hash["timers"]["macros"] = raw_macros.each_with_object({}) { |(num, cmd), acc| acc[num.to_i] = cmd.to_s }
    settings_hash
  end

  def self.save_window_settings(settings)
    File.write(Timers.window_settings_path, settings.to_yaml)
  end

  def self.key(name)
    name.to_s.strip.downcase
  end

  def self.sanitize_xml(value)
    value.to_s.gsub("&", "&amp;").gsub("<", "&lt;").gsub(">", "&gt;").gsub("'", "&apos;").gsub('"', "&quot;")
  end

  # Saga's own h:mm:ss / m:ss convention (see the exp/status report style
  # duration formatting already used elsewhere) -- not effectsbar's
  # single-dominant-unit "3h"/"45m" style, deliberately, to match the
  # native Active Spells/Cooldowns dialog this panel is modeled on.
  def self.format_duration(seconds)
    return "" if seconds.nil? || seconds <= 0

    total = seconds.to_i
    hours = total / 3600
    minutes = (total % 3600) / 60
    secs = total % 60

    hours > 0 ? format("%d:%02d:%02d", hours, minutes, secs) : format("%d:%02d", minutes, secs)
  end

  # 10-second buckets for duration sorting (see category_entries) --
  # Float::INFINITY (indefinite-duration entries) can't be floored, so it's
  # passed through as-is; it already sorts as the "highest" bucket either
  # way.
  def self.duration_bucket(seconds)
    return Float::INFINITY if seconds.infinite?

    (seconds / 10.0).floor
  end

  def self.set_missing_position!(position)
    return false unless %w[top bottom].include?(position)

    settings = load_window_settings
    self.missing_position = position
    settings["timers"]["missing_position"] = position
    save_window_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  def self.set_sort_mode!(mode)
    return false unless SORT_MODES.include?(mode)

    settings = load_window_settings
    self.sort_mode = mode
    settings["timers"]["sort_mode"] = mode
    save_window_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  def self.set_name_display!(mode)
    return false unless NAME_DISPLAYS.include?(mode)

    settings = load_window_settings
    self.name_display = mode
    settings["timers"]["name_display"] = mode
    save_window_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  # What a row actually shows for a given entry name, per *tm display. Falls
  # back to the plain name whenever Spell[] can't resolve it (most buffs/
  # debuffs/cooldowns aren't real spells), so "number"/"both" never render
  # a blank row.
  def self.display_text(name)
    case name_display
    when "number"
      spell = Spell[name]
      spell ? spell.num.to_s : name
    when "both"
      spell = Spell[name]
      spell ? "#{spell.num} #{name}" : name
    else
      name
    end
  rescue StandardError
    name
  end

  def self.toggle_panel_headers!
    settings = load_window_settings
    self.panel_headers = !panel_headers
    settings["timers"]["panel_headers"] = panel_headers
    save_window_settings(settings)
    panel_headers
  end

  # *tm headers -- the main "<icon> Category - Click to Track All" header
  # row per category (default on). Distinct from *tm pheaders, which is the
  # spell-circle sub-headers. Each row's own icon (leftmost column) still
  # identifies its category either way, so turning this off just removes
  # the header text/click-to-track-all row, not the per-row identification.
  def self.toggle_category_headers!
    settings = load_window_settings
    self.category_headers = !category_headers
    settings["timers"]["category_headers"] = category_headers
    save_window_settings(settings)
    category_headers
  end

  # *tm <#> <command chain> -- registers a ">"-separated command chain
  # against a spell number. When that spell is in Missing Spells, its name
  # becomes clickable (instead of plain text) and runs this chain, one
  # command per ">"-delimited step. Intended for "recast + prep" macros
  # like combining a store-all chain with getting/rubbing/stowing a prep
  # item -- see the header docstring for the exact example this was built
  # for.
  def self.set_macro!(num, command_chain)
    settings = load_window_settings
    self.macros[num] = command_chain
    settings["timers"]["macros"] = macros
    save_window_settings(settings)
  end

  # Returns false if num had no macro registered.
  def self.remove_macro!(num)
    return false unless macros.key?(num)

    settings = load_window_settings
    macros.delete(num)
    settings["timers"]["macros"] = macros
    save_window_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  # Runs the registered macro for num, one ">"-delimited step at a time,
  # with a short pause between steps so they don't all hit the game in the
  # same network burst. Returns false if nothing is registered for num.
  def self.run_macro(num)
    chain = macros[num]
    return false unless chain

    chain.split(/\s*>\s*/).each do |step|
      step = step.strip
      next if step.empty?

      put step
      sleep 0.3
    end
    true
  end

  # Spell circle number for a spell number, e.g. 1109 -> 11 (Empath) -- the
  # leading digits before the last two, same scheme Lich::Gemstone::Spells.
  # get_circle_name expects and the same one the game's own "spell all"
  # report groups by.
  def self.circle_num(num)
    num / 100
  end

  # Circle display name for an entry name, or nil if it isn't a real spell
  # (most buffs/debuffs aren't) -- callers group those under their own
  # "Other" bucket rather than skipping them.
  def self.circle_name(name_or_num)
    spell = Spell[name_or_num]
    return nil unless spell

    Lich::Gemstone::Spells.get_circle_name(circle_num(spell.num))
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  # Regroups a flat [[name, duration], ...] list (already in the caller's
  # chosen sort order) into [[circle_label, [[name, duration], ...]], ...],
  # circle order ascending (lowest circle number first, "Other" last for
  # anything Spell[] can't resolve), preserving each entry's relative order
  # within its own circle.
  def self.group_by_circle(entries)
    buckets = Hash.new { |h, k| h[k] = [] }
    entries.each do |name, duration|
      spell = Spell[name]
      key = spell ? circle_num(spell.num) : :other
      buckets[key] << [name, duration]
    end

    numbered = buckets.keys.reject { |k| k == :other }.sort
    ordered_keys = numbered + (buckets.key?(:other) ? [:other] : [])
    ordered_keys.map do |key|
      label = key == :other ? "Other" : Lich::Gemstone::Spells.get_circle_name(key)
      [label, buckets[key]]
    end
  rescue StandardError
    [["Other", entries]]
  end

  # Returns false (and does nothing) if name was already hidden, true if it
  # was actually newly added -- so callers can tell "just hid this" apart
  # from "was already hidden" instead of always reporting success.
  def self.add_ignored!(name)
    key = Timers.key(name)
    return false if ignored.include?(key)

    settings = load_window_settings
    self.ignored |= [key]
    settings["timers"]["ignored"] = ignored
    save_window_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  # Returns false (and does nothing) if name wasn't hidden to begin with.
  def self.remove_ignored!(name)
    key = Timers.key(name)
    return false unless ignored.include?(key)

    settings = load_window_settings
    self.ignored -= [key]
    settings["timers"]["ignored"] = ignored
    save_window_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  def self.unignore_all!
    settings = load_window_settings
    self.ignored = []
    settings["timers"]["ignored"] = []
    save_window_settings(settings)
  end

  # Returns false (and does nothing) if spell was already tracked, true if
  # it was actually newly added -- same reasoning as add_ignored!.
  def self.track!(spell)
    return false if tracked.include?(spell.num)

    settings = load_window_settings
    self.tracked |= [spell.num]
    settings["timers"]["tracked"] = tracked
    save_window_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  # Returns false (and does nothing) if num wasn't tracked to begin with.
  def self.untrack!(num)
    return false unless tracked.include?(num)

    settings = load_window_settings
    self.tracked -= [num]
    settings["timers"]["tracked"] = tracked
    save_window_settings(settings)
    true
  end

  def self.untrack_all!
    settings = load_window_settings
    self.tracked = []
    settings["timers"]["tracked"] = []
    save_window_settings(settings)
  end

  # Same source as category_entries, but WITHOUT the ignored-list filter --
  # "ignored" means "hide from the live categories," not "exclude from
  # ever being trackable," so track-all operations need the raw active
  # list, not the display-filtered one. Names only.
  def self.active_names(category)
    if category == :spells
      claimed = Timers.other_category_names
      Spell.active.map(&:name).reject { |name| claimed.include?(Timers.key(name)) }
    else
      registry = case category
                 when :buffs then Effects::Buffs
                 when :debuffs then Effects::Debuffs
                 when :cooldowns then Effects::Cooldowns
                 end
      return [] unless registry

      registry.to_h.keys.select { |name| name.is_a?(String) }
    end
  rescue StandardError
    []
  end

  # *tm track all -- everything currently active across all 4 categories
  # (the same set "spell active" reports as Spells/Cooldowns/Buffs/
  # Debuffs), not just Active Spells. Same Spell[] resolution as
  # *tm trackall <category>/clicking a header, just for every category at
  # once. Returns how many were actually added.
  def self.track_all!
    added = 0
    CATEGORY_ORDER.each do |category|
      active_names(category).each do |name|
        spell = Spell[name]
        next unless spell

        added += 1 if track!(spell)
      end
    end
    added
  end

  # Every string-keyed name currently in Effects::Buffs/Debuffs/Cooldowns,
  # lowercased -- what category_entries(:spells) excludes from Spell.active
  # so something like Celerity (a spell mechanically, but a Buff as far as
  # the game's own dialogs are concerned) doesn't show up in both Active
  # Spells and Buffs at once.
  def self.other_category_names
    (Effects::Buffs.to_h.keys + Effects::Debuffs.to_h.keys + Effects::Cooldowns.to_h.keys)
      .select { |name| name.is_a?(String) }
      .map { |name| Timers.key(name) }
  rescue StandardError
    []
  end

  # [name, duration] pairs for everything currently active in the given
  # category, minus anything on the ignored list. Order follows
  # Timers.sort_mode (*tm sort az/za/dhigh/dlow) -- these can hold a couple
  # dozen entries at once (see the screenshot this panel was built from),
  # so a stable, scannable order matters more than "order applied."
  #
  # :spells uses Spell.active (lib/common/spell.rb -- same thing
  # Lich::Gemstone::Spells.active calls), not Effects::Spells. The Active
  # Spells *dialog* feed (Effects::Spells) can carry some active spells as
  # integer-keyed entries only, depending on the player's spell-name
  # display preference -- those got silently dropped by the
  # name.is_a?(String) filter every other category still needs, so
  # "Active Spells" (and *tm track all/trackall spells, which reads this
  # same method) under-counted against what "spell active" or
  # Spell.active actually report. Spell.active doesn't have that gap.
  def self.category_entries(category)
    now = Time.now.to_f
    entries = []

    if category == :spells
      # Spell.active includes things the game itself categorizes as a Buff
      # (Celerity/506 being the one that surfaced this -- it's in the
      # native Buffs dialog, never Active Spells), so anything currently
      # claimed by Buffs/Debuffs/Cooldowns is excluded here rather than
      # letting it double up in both sections. Those 3 registries stay the
      # authority on their own category; Spell.active is only needed to
      # fill the Active Spells gap Effects::Spells itself has.
      claimed = Timers.other_category_names
      Spell.active.each do |spell|
        next if Timers.ignored.include?(Timers.key(spell.name))
        next if claimed.include?(Timers.key(spell.name))

        remaining = spell.secsleft.to_f
        next if remaining <= 0

        entries << [spell.name, Timers.format_duration(remaining), remaining]
      end
    else
      registry = case category
                 when :buffs then Effects::Buffs
                 when :debuffs then Effects::Debuffs
                 when :cooldowns then Effects::Cooldowns
                 end
      return [] unless registry

      registry.to_h.each do |name, expires_at|
        next unless name.is_a?(String)
        next if Timers.ignored.include?(Timers.key(name))

        remaining = expires_at.to_f - now
        next if remaining <= 0 && expires_at.to_f != 0

        duration_secs = expires_at.to_f == 0 ? Float::INFINITY : remaining
        duration = expires_at.to_f == 0 ? "" : Timers.format_duration(remaining)
        entries << [name, duration, duration_secs]
      end
    end

    sorted = case Timers.sort_mode
             when "name_desc"     then entries.sort_by { |name, _duration, _secs| name }.reverse
             # Bucketed to the nearest 10s (name as tiebreak within a
             # bucket) instead of raw seconds -- sorting by exact remaining
             # time reorders the whole list nearly every poll as durations
             # tick down, which reads as constant jitter rather than a
             # stable "by duration" view. Two entries under 10s apart don't
             # swap places; only a real gap moves something.
             when "duration_asc"  then entries.sort_by { |name, _duration, secs| [Timers.duration_bucket(secs), name] }
             when "duration_desc" then entries.sort_by { |name, _duration, secs| [-Timers.duration_bucket(secs), name] }
             else                      entries.sort_by { |name, _duration, _secs| name }
             end

    sorted.map { |name, duration, _secs| [name, duration] }
  rescue StandardError
    []
  end

  # [num, name] pairs for every tracked spell that ISN'T currently active,
  # minus anything on the ignored list. Uses Spell[] (lib/common/spell.rb),
  # Lich's own spell tracking, rather than Effects::Spells -- so this stays
  # accurate even if the Active Spells dialog hasn't been (re)opened.
  def self.missing_entries
    tracked.map do |num|
      spell = Spell[num]
      next nil unless spell
      next nil if spell.active?
      next nil if Timers.ignored.include?(Timers.key(spell.name))

      [spell.num, spell.name]
    end.compact.sort_by { |_num, name| name }
  rescue StandardError
    []
  end

  def self.snapshot
    entries = Timers::CATEGORY_ORDER.flat_map { |category| Timers.category_entries(category) }
    entries += Timers.missing_entries
    entries.map { |a, b| "#{a}|#{b}" }
  rescue StandardError
    []
  end

  def self.build_dialog
    out = String.new("<dialogData id='Timers' clear='t'>")
    top = 0

    render_missing = lambda do
      missing = Timers.missing_entries
      next if missing.empty?

      out << "<label id='tm_missing_header' value='&#x2757; Missing Spells' justify='left' left='0' top='#{top}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
      top += Timers::ROW_HEIGHT
      missing.each do |num, name|
        out << "<label id='tm_missing_icon_#{num}' value='#{Timers::MISSING_ICON}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{top}' width='#{Timers::ICON_WIDTH}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        display = Timers.sanitize_xml(Timers.display_text(name))
        if Timers.macros.key?(num)
          # A macro is registered for this spell -- name becomes clickable
          # and runs it (*tm run <#>) instead of sitting as plain text.
          out << "<link id='tm_missing_name_#{num}' value='#{display}' cmd='*tm run #{num}' justify='left' left='#{Timers::NAME_LEFT}' top='#{top}' width='#{Timers::NAME_WIDTH}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        else
          out << "<label id='tm_missing_name_#{num}' value='#{display}' justify='left' left='#{Timers::NAME_LEFT}' top='#{top}' width='#{Timers::NAME_WIDTH}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        end
        out << "<link id='tm_missing_x_#{num}' value='#{Timers::REMOVE_ICON}' cmd='*tm untrack #{num}' justify='left' left='#{Timers::REMOVE_LEFT}' top='#{top}' width='#{Timers::REMOVE_WIDTH}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        top += Timers::ROW_HEIGHT
      end
    end

    render_missing.call if Timers.missing_position == "top"

    render_row = lambda do |category, name, duration, row_id|
      track_cmd = "*tm track #{Timers.sanitize_xml(name)}"
      ignore_cmd = "*tm ignore #{Timers.sanitize_xml(Timers.key(name))}"
      out << "<label id='tm_icon_#{row_id}' value='#{Timers::CATEGORY_ICONS[category]}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{top}' width='#{Timers::ICON_WIDTH}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
      out << "<link id='tm_name_#{row_id}' value='#{Timers.sanitize_xml(Timers.display_text(name))}' cmd='#{track_cmd}' justify='left' left='#{Timers::NAME_LEFT}' top='#{top}' width='#{Timers::NAME_WIDTH}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
      out << "<label id='tm_dur_#{row_id}' value='#{Timers.sanitize_xml(duration)}' justify='left' left='#{Timers::DURATION_LEFT}' top='#{top}' width='#{Timers::DURATION_WIDTH}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
      out << "<link id='tm_x_#{row_id}' value='#{Timers::REMOVE_ICON}' cmd='#{ignore_cmd}' justify='left' left='#{Timers::REMOVE_LEFT}' top='#{top}' width='#{Timers::REMOVE_WIDTH}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
      top += Timers::ROW_HEIGHT
    end

    Timers::CATEGORY_ORDER.each do |category|
      entries = Timers.category_entries(category)
      next if entries.empty?

      if Timers.category_headers
        header_cmd = "*tm trackall #{category}"
        out << "<link id='tm_header_#{category}' value='#{Timers::CATEGORY_LABELS[category]}' cmd='#{header_cmd}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{top}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' />"
        top += Timers::ROW_HEIGHT
      end

      if Timers.panel_headers
        idx = 0
        Timers.group_by_circle(entries).each do |circle_label, circle_entries|
          out << "<label id='tm_circle_#{category}_#{idx}' value='#{Timers.sanitize_xml(circle_label)}' justify='left' left='#{Timers::NAME_LEFT}' top='#{top}' height='#{Timers::ROW_HEIGHT}' font='small' />"
          top += Timers::ROW_HEIGHT
          circle_entries.each do |name, duration|
            render_row.call(category, name, duration, "#{category}_#{idx}")
            idx += 1
          end
        end
      else
        entries.each_with_index do |(name, duration), idx|
          render_row.call(category, name, duration, "#{category}_#{idx}")
        end
      end
    end

    render_missing.call if Timers.missing_position == "bottom"

    if top.zero?
      out << "<label id='tm_none' value='Nothing active or missing' justify='left' left='0' top='0' />"
    end

    out << "</dialogData>"
    out
  end
end

@tm_settings = Timers.load_window_settings
Timers.tracked = @tm_settings["timers"]["tracked"]
Timers.ignored = @tm_settings["timers"]["ignored"]
Timers.missing_position = @tm_settings["timers"]["missing_position"]
Timers.sort_mode = @tm_settings["timers"]["sort_mode"]
Timers.name_display = @tm_settings["timers"]["name_display"]
Timers.panel_headers = @tm_settings["timers"]["panel_headers"]
Timers.macros = @tm_settings["timers"]["macros"]
Timers.category_headers = @tm_settings["timers"]["category_headers"]

tm_upstream_hook_id = "#{Script.current.name}_upstream"
UpstreamHook.remove(tm_upstream_hook_id) rescue nil
UpstreamHook.add(tm_upstream_hook_id, proc do |command|
  if command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+track\s+all\b/i
    added = Timers.track_all!
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
    respond "Timers: added #{added} new spell(s) to the watch list"
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+track\s+(.+?)\s*\z/i
    requested = Regexp.last_match(1)
    spell = Spell[requested]
    if spell
      if Timers.track!(spell)
        _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
        respond "Timers now watching: #{spell.name} (#{spell.num})"
      else
        respond "Timers: already watching #{spell.name} (#{spell.num})"
      end
    else
      respond "Timers: could not find a spell matching '#{requested}'"
    end
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+untrack\s+all\b/i
    Timers.untrack_all!
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
    respond "Timers: no longer watching anything"
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+untrack\s+(.+?)\s*\z/i
    requested = Regexp.last_match(1)
    spell = Spell[requested]
    num = spell ? spell.num : requested.to_i
    if Timers.untrack!(num)
      _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
      respond "Timers: no longer watching ##{num}"
    else
      respond "Timers: wasn't watching ##{num}"
    end
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+tracked\s*\z/i
    if Timers.tracked.empty?
      respond "Timers: not watching any spells"
    else
      respond "Timers watch list:"
      by_circle = Timers.tracked.sort.group_by { |num| Timers.circle_num(num) }
      by_circle.keys.sort.each do |circle|
        respond "  #{Lich::Gemstone::Spells.get_circle_name(circle)}:"
        by_circle[circle].each do |num|
          spell = Spell[num]
          respond "    #{num} #{spell ? spell.name : '(unknown)'}"
        end
      end
    end
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+trackall\s+(spells|buffs|debuffs|cooldowns)\b/i
    category = Regexp.last_match(1).downcase.to_sym
    added = 0
    Timers.active_names(category).each do |name|
      spell = Spell[name]
      next unless spell

      added += 1 if Timers.track!(spell)
    end
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
    respond "Timers: added #{added} new spell(s) from #{category} to the watch list"
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+ignore\s+(.+?)\s*\z/i
    requested = Regexp.last_match(1)
    # Resolve a spell number (or fuzzy name) to its real name first --
    # ignoring the literal string "1605" does nothing, since category
    # entries are matched by name text, never by number.
    spell = Spell[requested]
    name = spell ? spell.name : requested
    if Timers.add_ignored!(name)
      _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
      respond "Timers: hiding '#{name}'"
    else
      respond "Timers: already hiding '#{name}'"
    end
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+unignore\s+all\b/i
    Timers.unignore_all!
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
    respond "Timers: no longer hiding anything"
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+unignore\s+(.+?)\s*\z/i
    requested = Regexp.last_match(1)
    spell = Spell[requested]
    name = spell ? spell.name : requested
    if Timers.remove_ignored!(name)
      _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
      respond "Timers: no longer hiding '#{name}'"
    else
      respond "Timers: wasn't hiding '#{name}'"
    end
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+ignored\s*\z/i
    if Timers.ignored.empty?
      respond "Timers: nothing hidden"
    else
      respond "Timers hidden names:"
      resolved = []
      unresolved = []
      Timers.ignored.sort.each do |key|
        spell = Spell[key]
        spell ? resolved << spell : unresolved << key
      end
      by_circle = resolved.group_by { |spell| Timers.circle_num(spell.num) }
      by_circle.keys.sort.each do |circle|
        respond "  #{Lich::Gemstone::Spells.get_circle_name(circle)}:"
        by_circle[circle].sort_by(&:num).each { |spell| respond "    #{spell.num} #{spell.name}" }
      end
      unless unresolved.empty?
        respond "  Other:"
        unresolved.each { |key| respond "    #{key}" }
      end
    end
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+missing\s+(top|bottom)\b/i
    position = Regexp.last_match(1).downcase
    Timers.set_missing_position!(position)
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
    respond "Timers: Missing Spells now shown at the #{position}"
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+sort\s+(az|za|dhigh|dlow)\b/i
    mode = { "az" => "name_asc", "za" => "name_desc", "dhigh" => "duration_desc", "dlow" => "duration_asc" }[Regexp.last_match(1).downcase]
    Timers.set_sort_mode!(mode)
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
    respond "Timers: sort order is now #{mode}"
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+display\s+(name|number|both)\b/i
    mode = Regexp.last_match(1).downcase
    Timers.set_name_display!(mode)
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
    respond "Timers: name display is now #{mode}"
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+pheaders\b/i
    enabled = Timers.toggle_panel_headers!
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
    respond "Timers: spell circle headers in panel: #{enabled ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+headers\b/i
    enabled = Timers.toggle_category_headers!
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
    respond "Timers: category headers in panel: #{enabled ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+run\s+(\d+)\b/i
    num = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    if Timers.run_macro(num)
      respond "Timers: running macro for ##{num}"
    else
      respond "Timers: no macro registered for ##{num}"
    end
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+clearmacro\s+(\d+)\b/i
    num = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    if Timers.remove_macro!(num)
      _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
      respond "Timers: removed macro for ##{num}"
    else
      respond "Timers: no macro registered for ##{num}"
    end
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+macros\s*\z/i
    if Timers.macros.empty?
      respond "Timers: no macros registered"
    else
      respond "Timers macros:"
      Timers.macros.keys.sort.each do |num|
        spell = Spell[num]
        respond "  #{num} #{spell ? spell.name : '(unknown)'}: #{Timers.macros[num]}"
      end
    end
    nil
  elsif command.strip =~ /\*tm\s+(\d+)\s+(.+)\z/i
    num = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    chain = Regexp.last_match(2).strip
    Timers.set_macro!(num, chain)
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
    spell = Spell[num]
    respond "Timers: macro set for ##{num}#{spell ? " (#{spell.name})" : ''}: #{chain}"
    nil
  else
    command
  end
end)

_respond("<closeDialog id='Timers'/><openDialog type='dynamic' id='Timers' title='Timers' target='Timers' scroll='manual' location='main' resident='true'><dialogData id='Timers'></dialogData></openDialog>")
_respond(Timers.build_dialog)

before_dying do
  UpstreamHook.remove(tm_upstream_hook_id) rescue nil
  _respond("<closeDialog id='Timers'/>")
end

echo "Timers is active."

@tm_last_snapshot = Timers.snapshot
@tm_last_refresh_at = Time.now

loop do
  snapshot = Timers.snapshot
  if snapshot != @tm_last_snapshot || (Time.now - @tm_last_refresh_at) > 5.0
    @tm_last_snapshot = snapshot
    @tm_last_refresh_at = Time.now
    _respond(Timers.build_dialog)
  end
  sleep 0.5
end
